		(object Operation "SolveSqr3"
		    attributes 	(list Attribute_Set)
		    quid       	"37BD38C2014F"
		    documentation 	
|Solves the Square Equation with three Parameters: a*x^2 + b*x + c = 0
|	 * x1 and x2 are ByRef Parameters that contain the two Solutions. 
|	 * The Return Value determines whether there is a real Solution or not.	 
		    
		    parameters 	(list Parameters
			(object Parameter "a"
			    type       	"MetricIRing")
			(object Parameter "b"
			    type       	"MetricIRing")
			(object Parameter "c"
			    type       	"MetricIRing")
			(object Parameter "x1"
			    type       	"MetricIRing")
			(object Parameter "x2"
			    type       	"MetricIRing"))
		    result     	"boolean"
		    concurrency 	"Sequential"
		    opExportControl 	"Public"
		    uid        	0)
		(object Operation "SolveSqr2"
		    attributes 	(list Attribute_Set)
		    quid       	"37BD38C70233"
		    documentation 	
|Solves the normed Square Equation with two Parameters: x^2 + b*x + c = 0
|	 * x1 and x2 are ByRef Parameters that contain the two Solutions. 
|	 * The Return Value determines whether there is a real Solution or not.
|	 * If not, the real Part is returned in x1 and the imaginary Part in x2.
|	 * If yes, x1 contains the larger absolute Value.
|	 * This also results in higher Accuracy, because no cancelling takes place.	 
		    
		    parameters 	(list Parameters
			(object Parameter "b"
			    type       	"MetricIRing")
			(object Parameter "c"
			    type       	"MetricIRing")
			(object Parameter "x1"
			    type       	"MetricIRing")
			(object Parameter "x2"
			    type       	"MetricIRing"))
		    result     	"boolean"
		    concurrency 	"Sequential"
		    opExportControl 	"Public"
		    uid        	0)
		(object Operation "Combination"
		    attributes 	(list Attribute_Set)
		    quid       	"37BD38CA0223"
		    documentation 	
|Calculates the Combination(n,k) = n!/(k!*(n-k)!)
|	 * This is the number of Samples with Size k from a Set of n Elements,
|	 * without considering the Sequence.
|	 * It is also used with real n on calculating the Power Series 
|	 * of 'small' Disturbances: (1+-x)^m = 1 +- mx + ... + Comb(m,k)(+-x)^k
|	 * 
|	 * This Calculation is optimized only in MetricIRing, 
|	 * because Comb(n, k) == Comb (n, n-k) (but only for integer n!!!).
|	 * The only Problem is that for large n and k 
|	 * the Division takes place after the Calculation of Vari(n, k),
|	 * which may result in an Overflow.	 
		    
		    parameters 	(list Parameters
			(object Parameter "k"
			    type       	"IntegrityRing"))
		    result     	"IntegrityRing"
		    concurrency 	"Sequential"
		    opExportControl 	"Public"
		    uid        	0)
		(object Operation "dblFactAt"
		    attributes 	(list Attribute_Set)
		    quid       	"37BD38CB004E"
		    documentation 	
|Calculates the Double Faculty of this integer number in Place.
|	 * The Definition is recursive: 
|	 * n!! = dblFact(n) = n * dblFact(n-2); Fact(0) = Fact(1) = 1;	 
		    
		    result     	"IntegrityRing"
		    concurrency 	"Sequential"
		    opExportControl 	"Public"
		    uid        	0)
		(object Operation "p_Norm"
		    attributes 	(list Attribute_Set)
		    quid       	"37BD38CB0058"
		    documentation 	
|p-Norm: Defined as Sum(|x|^p)^1/p
|	 * Generic Norm: the other Norms are Special Cases:
|	 * In 1-dimensional Spaces all Norms fall together.	 
		    
		    parameters 	(list Parameters
			(object Parameter "p"
			    type       	"double"))
		    result     	"MetricIRing"
		    concurrency 	"Sequential"
		    opExportControl 	"Public"
		    uid        	0)
